Suneo, what's in your hands?

544
00:30:37,302 --> 00:30:39,805
It's picture of my favorite singer idol
Mazi! Let me have a look.

545
00:30:39,871 --> 00:30:42,613
No! This is my favorite picture
with her signature on.

546
00:30:43,174 --> 00:30:44,983
What do these photos mean?

547
00:30:45,009 --> 00:30:48,218
Oh, I can see Mazi's vocal
concert free of charge.

548
00:30:48,246 --> 00:30:50,692
Can I? Free of charge?

549
00:30:50,715 --> 00:30:52,126
I want to see too.

550
00:30:52,150 --> 00:30:53,493
I want to see.

551
00:30:53,518 --> 00:30:56,158
But you didn't lend me
the book of 'Comic Boy'

552
00:30:56,187 --> 00:30:57,666
Don't say so!

553
00:30:57,722 --> 00:30:59,793
I'm her faithful movie fan!

554
00:30:59,858 --> 00:31:03,237
Then you'll lend me the cartoon later?

555
00:31:03,261 --> 00:31:05,502
Yeah, I will. I will lend it to you.

556
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:08,977
Not only the cartons, but also the
model toys, I'll send to you.

557
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:11,947
So we have no ways.

558
00:31:11,970 --> 00:31:13,608
Wait!

559
00:31:14,405 --> 00:31:16,783
You can see it anytime
as long as you have this ticket.

560
00:31:16,808 --> 00:31:18,583
Thank you, Nobita!

561
00:31:19,711 --> 00:31:21,713
Is it true?

562
00:31:24,282 --> 00:31:25,989
It's already midnight! Get up soon!

563
00:31:26,017 --> 00:31:27,496
I still want to sleep.

564
00:31:27,518 --> 00:31:29,623
We must set all of them during tonight.

565
00:31:37,161 --> 00:31:39,505
Where shall we start to set first?

566
00:31:41,933 --> 00:31:43,435
How can we get in?

567
00:31:43,501 --> 00:31:45,981
Get in through the passage.

568
00:31:46,037 --> 00:31:47,744
Come on!

569
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:50,617
Is it okay to set it here?

570
00:31:50,642 --> 00:31:51,950
Yeah!

571
00:31:52,644 --> 00:31:54,646
Now it's the cinema!

572
00:31:55,213 --> 00:31:57,693
It's Outspace Shark
that Shizuka asked for.

573
00:31:58,549 --> 00:32:00,119
Well,

574
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:03,399
where shall I set it?

575
00:32:03,454 --> 00:32:04,956
It shall be set on a pantoscopic place.

576
00:32:05,023 --> 00:32:07,333
Who's that man over there?

577
00:32:07,692 --> 00:32:10,639
What's he doing there?

578
00:32:10,662 --> 00:32:12,642
Hey, wait! Don't run!

579
00:32:12,664 --> 00:32:14,701
Run quickly, take it easy...

580
00:32:14,766 --> 00:32:16,803
Didn't I tell you not to run?
Didn't you hear that?

581
00:32:16,868 --> 00:32:18,745
We're not bad eggs.

582
00:32:18,770 --> 00:32:21,114
We are good eggs in fact.

583
00:32:21,139 --> 00:32:22,846
Help me! Get into it soon...

584
00:32:22,874 --> 00:32:24,717
Where to go?

585
00:32:25,576 --> 00:32:28,386
So dangerous! I didn't expect
that there would have guards.

586
00:32:28,413 --> 00:32:31,360
But I've installed the autodyne!

587
00:32:31,382 --> 00:32:33,453
That's Doraemon!

588
00:32:34,652 --> 00:32:37,633
Geez! Who is that?

589
00:32:40,425 --> 00:32:42,427
Here's the Eden Ball Park

590
00:32:42,493 --> 00:32:44,973
Set some autodyne inside and outside
the field, and some behind the Gallery

591
00:32:45,029 --> 00:32:47,009
So the lens can be switch!

592
00:32:47,365 --> 00:32:49,436
This time you must
pay more attention to guards.

593
00:32:49,801 --> 00:32:52,645
There will be a show of Outspace Shark
in Nobita's home.

594
00:32:52,670 --> 00:32:53,944
Really?

595
00:32:53,972 --> 00:32:55,849
He invited us all to come to see.

596
00:32:58,776 --> 00:33:00,255
I've been waiting for you so long.

597
00:33:00,278 --> 00:33:01,757
Please come in to have a seat.

598
00:33:01,779 --> 00:33:03,349
Come in, please!

599
00:33:03,414 --> 00:33:05,416
It'll be shown now.

600
00:33:05,483 --> 00:33:07,463
Strange! It's not shown on it.

601
00:33:07,518 --> 00:33:09,327
Won't it...

602
00:33:09,354 --> 00:33:11,334
Doraemon, what's wrong?

603
00:33:11,389 --> 00:33:12,834
No films on it.

604
00:33:12,857 --> 00:33:17,135
I am thinking if it will be...

605
00:33:17,161 --> 00:33:18,538
I made a mistake.

606
00:33:18,563 --> 00:33:20,736
I transposed the autodyne
and the communication facility.

607
00:33:20,765 --> 00:33:21,937
It's crap now...

608
00:33:21,966 --> 00:33:26,437
What! So we've been shown on the screen?

609
00:33:32,243 --> 00:33:36,020
Story of snow-mountain.

610
00:33:37,248 --> 00:33:40,229
Shizuka, I have something to
talk to you! What's it?

611
00:33:40,284 --> 00:33:43,561
Come to my home to do
your homework with me.

612
00:33:43,588 --> 00:33:44,862
Oh, I won't.

613
00:33:44,889 --> 00:33:49,360
You said to do homework with me every
time, but you always copy my answers.

614
00:33:50,695 --> 00:33:51,673
I'm back!

615
00:33:51,729 --> 00:33:53,140
Welcome back!

616
00:33:53,164 --> 00:33:56,077
Now I'm getting more and more worried!

617
00:33:56,100 --> 00:33:57,545
What are you worry about?

618
00:33:57,568 --> 00:34:02,916
The searching result shows by the Time
Machine is I'll marry Shizuka, right?

619
00:34:02,940 --> 00:34:06,752
But I always don't think so.

620
00:34:06,778 --> 00:34:10,624
Actually I feel it's unimaginable!

621
00:34:10,648 --> 00:34:13,026
Such a good girl,
how will he be so foolish

622
00:34:13,051 --> 00:34:14,894
to like Nobita?

623
00:34:14,919 --> 00:34:17,866
There're so many boys better than Nobita.

624
00:34:18,823 --> 00:34:20,131
You did go too far!

625
00:34:20,158 --> 00:34:21,728
Don't be excited...

626
00:34:21,793 --> 00:34:27,471
And about that if you can marry Shizuka,
you want to confirm, right?

627
00:34:27,498 --> 00:34:29,478
I know...

628
00:34:29,801 --> 00:34:31,371
It's this!

629
00:34:31,436 --> 00:34:33,473
Time TV!

630
00:34:33,538 --> 00:34:35,882
14 years later, on the date of Oct. 25,

631
00:34:35,907 --> 00:34:39,286
Nobita and Shizuka got married.

632
00:34:39,310 --> 00:34:42,018
So let's see the earlier situation.

633
00:34:43,014 --> 00:34:44,823
It's adult Nobita!

634
00:34:47,218 --> 00:34:49,129
Very ordinary!

635
00:34:49,153 --> 00:34:51,292
That's Shizuka.

636
00:34:51,322 --> 00:34:55,065
Hurry to decide! Go or not!

637
00:34:55,093 --> 00:34:56,595
I do want to go,

638
00:34:56,661 --> 00:34:58,004
but I'm not good at climbing the slope.

639
00:34:58,029 --> 00:35:00,202
If it's the smooth ghat,
I'll have no problem.

640
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:03,409
You're not patient at all.

641
00:35:03,835 --> 00:35:05,746
Then forget it.

642
00:35:05,770 --> 00:35:07,943
I'll go with another friend.

643
00:35:07,972 --> 00:35:10,543
Well...Shizuka.

644
00:35:10,842 --> 00:35:13,482
I can't bear with it.
Let's watch the later status.

645
00:35:13,511 --> 00:35:14,819
Yep.

646
00:35:15,980 --> 00:35:17,516
Stage...

647
00:35:17,582 --> 00:35:19,584
Shizuka is alone.

648
00:35:21,152 --> 00:35:23,359
She must get lost with her friends.

649
00:35:23,721 --> 00:35:27,191
At that time where's the adult Nobita?
What is he doing?

650
00:35:27,558 --> 00:35:30,505
He's lying in bed
since he got a serious cold.

651
00:35:33,464 --> 00:35:35,375
Really boring.

652
00:35:37,201 --> 00:35:38,839
Wait, right!

653
00:35:38,870 --> 00:35:40,611
It goes like this!

654
00:35:40,638 --> 00:35:42,447
In this case the riddle is uncovered.

655
00:35:42,473 --> 00:35:45,215
Lend me the Time Cloth, hurry!

656
00:35:45,243 --> 00:35:46,745
Okay!

657
00:35:55,153 --> 00:35:58,600
Next, I'll go to save Shizuka
by the Time Machine.

658
00:35:58,656 --> 00:36:00,260
Shizuka will be very touched.

659
00:36:00,324 --> 00:36:02,304
Then say 'What a reliable man'!

660
00:36:02,360 --> 00:36:03,805
By this chance she will marry me.

661
00:36:03,828 --> 00:36:06,001
That must be like this. Really perfect!

662
00:36:06,731 --> 00:36:08,711
Don't come to help!

663
00:36:08,766 --> 00:36:11,747
I'll save her by myself.
You mustn't come.

664
00:36:12,904 --> 00:36:14,884
No problem?

665
00:36:16,440 --> 00:36:18,420
I'll marry...

666
00:36:20,711 --> 00:36:24,056
Shizuka, hey...

667
00:36:24,849 --> 00:36:28,228
Nobita, you're coming!

668
00:36:28,653 --> 00:36:30,894
As long as with me, you needn't worry.

669
00:36:31,522 --> 00:36:33,024
Let me carry the luggage.

670
00:36:33,090 --> 00:36:34,034
No, thanks anyway.

671
00:36:34,058 --> 00:36:36,470
It doesn't matter, don't hold back.

672
00:36:40,398 --> 00:36:42,935
Let me carry it.

673
00:36:43,901 --> 00:36:46,006
Too ashamed!

674
00:36:46,904 --> 00:36:49,680
We can't walk at will when we suffered
the trouble in the mountain.

675
00:36:49,707 --> 00:36:52,381
We must confirm the directions
by the map.

676
00:36:53,811 --> 00:36:54,983
Gosh!

677
00:36:55,012 --> 00:36:56,821
You've taken the wrong map.

678
00:36:56,847 --> 00:36:59,191
It's really like your work-style.

679
00:36:59,217 --> 00:37:01,527
It doesn't matter.
The roadsign will tell us how to go.

680
00:37:01,552 --> 00:37:03,031
<i>Let's gm!</i>

681
00:37:03,087 --> 00:37:05,158
That's okay.

682
00:37:10,428 --> 00:37:13,739
There's a cave over there,
let's have a rest.

683
00:37:13,764 --> 00:37:14,834
Good idea!

684
00:37:14,899 --> 00:37:17,402
Have a rest, have a rest...

685
00:37:20,905 --> 00:37:23,852
When we suffer the trouble in the snow
mountain, the coldness is horrible.

686
00:37:23,874 --> 00:37:26,150
Let me start a fire to warm us.

687
00:37:26,177 --> 00:37:28,350
You must think the match has been wetted
and crinkled.

688
00:37:28,379 --> 00:37:30,359
Don't worry!

689
00:37:30,414 --> 00:37:33,122
I know how to start a fire.

690
00:37:33,818 --> 00:37:36,799
Shizuka,
please carry here some dried wood.

691
00:37:39,423 --> 00:37:41,664
Why don't start a fire?

692
00:37:41,692 --> 00:37:44,229
Do you need the Lighter?

693
00:37:44,295 --> 00:37:47,071
Why didn't you tell me
that you have the Lighter?!

694
00:37:47,098 --> 00:37:49,476
Seeing that you're in high spirit,
I didn't want to cool you.

695
00:37:52,670 --> 00:37:54,013
So cold!

696
00:37:54,038 --> 00:37:56,040
Really cold!

697
00:37:59,777 --> 00:38:03,088
Put on this, I'm okay.

698
00:38:03,114 --> 00:38:04,923
So cold!

699
00:38:05,249 --> 00:38:07,559
That's because you shouldn't have
come to the snow mountain in this.

700
00:38:07,585 --> 00:38:09,656
If you don't change your clothes,
you'll die!

701
00:38:09,720 --> 00:38:12,462
But I haven't any clothes to change.

702
00:38:12,490 --> 00:38:15,767
Lend you my carpet! Well, thank you.

703
00:38:15,793 --> 00:38:18,774
You've looked forward to that for long,
right? I've taken many tasty foods.

704
00:38:18,796 --> 00:38:20,366
Really, too great!

705
00:38:20,431 --> 00:38:22,468
There're the peach cans, beef cans,

706
00:38:22,533 --> 00:38:24,103
also the bean cans.

707
00:38:24,168 --> 00:38:26,148
Which one would you like to have?

708
00:38:26,170 --> 00:38:31,347
Haven't you brought so many cans,
but forgotten the opener?

709
00:38:34,979 --> 00:38:36,754
You hit home!

710
00:38:36,781 --> 00:38:39,955
There're still some dried meat balls
left. I'll share one with you.

711
00:38:44,021 --> 00:38:46,433
The dried meat balls?!

712
00:38:53,130 --> 00:38:55,838
The snow's stopped. Let's get going!

713
00:38:58,602 --> 00:39:00,843
Shizuka, watch out!

714
00:39:00,871 --> 00:39:03,750
The ground became very slithery.

715
00:39:06,644 --> 00:39:09,124
Nobita, are you okay?

716
00:39:09,580 --> 00:39:13,027
I got my glasses lost since I fell down.
So I can't move now!

717
00:39:13,417 --> 00:39:15,795
I've sent the SOS by radio.

718
00:39:15,820 --> 00:39:18,027
They're coming right now!
Pay more patience!

719
00:39:24,161 --> 00:39:26,641
We failed, it's hopeless!

720
00:39:26,964 --> 00:39:29,638
Next what shall we become like?

721
00:39:30,134 --> 00:39:32,114
Completely hopeless!

722
00:39:32,136 --> 00:39:35,117
I will to marry Nobita.

723
00:39:35,172 --> 00:39:37,379
Thank you.

724
00:39:37,408 --> 00:39:40,252
If I don't stay with you,
you'll get in danger.

725
00:39:40,277 --> 00:39:42,780
I can't have the heart to look at that.

726
00:39:44,215 --> 00:39:46,217
Such a coward, I don't like!

727
00:39:46,283 --> 00:39:47,261
I can't stand!

728
00:39:47,284 --> 00:39:50,925
You should try your best to
learn to be more manful.

729
00:39:50,955 --> 00:39:52,696
That's true.

730
00:39:59,597 --> 00:40:03,374
The Money bees are working hard!

731
00:40:11,175 --> 00:40:14,622
Nobita, you really like playing
the game of turning rope.

732
00:40:14,678 --> 00:40:17,488
Not very much.

733
00:40:17,515 --> 00:40:19,688
My pocket money was used up,

734
00:40:19,717 --> 00:40:21,458
but this game needn't money.

735
00:40:21,485 --> 00:40:23,931
A game which you won't
feel tired and hungry,

736
00:40:23,954 --> 00:40:26,230
is only this one.

737
00:40:26,590 --> 00:40:29,901
Nobita, would you like to
help me to clean the slot?

738
00:40:29,927 --> 00:40:32,373
Clean the slot?

739
00:40:32,396 --> 00:40:36,242
Gosh...l forgot to do my homework.

740
00:40:36,267 --> 00:40:39,680
I'm very busy. Mom, you can go to
ask Doraemon!

741
00:40:39,703 --> 00:40:41,683
How could you be?!

742
00:40:41,972 --> 00:40:44,452
That's very easy to be seen through.

743
00:40:44,508 --> 00:40:46,454
Nobita

744
00:40:46,477 --> 00:40:49,253
I'll do that...

745
00:40:52,983 --> 00:40:57,989
There's no money for such things,
really hateful!

746
00:40:58,055 --> 00:41:01,730
And it only can make me tired.

747
00:41:05,396 --> 00:41:07,034
What's this?

748
00:41:07,097 --> 00:41:08,735
100 yen!

749
00:41:08,766 --> 00:41:10,177
I can earn money!

750
00:41:10,201 --> 00:41:12,442
Cleaning the slot is really not bad.

751
00:41:13,304 --> 00:41:15,045
I'm home!

752
00:41:15,072 --> 00:41:17,313
Doraemon...

753
00:41:17,741 --> 00:41:19,652
Doraemon, a big discovery.

754
00:41:19,677 --> 00:41:22,920
What strange thing did you find?

755
00:41:24,081 --> 00:41:27,893
Such money sleeping somewhere unnoted
like this...

756
00:41:27,918 --> 00:41:31,422
should be a big sum in Japan, right?

757
00:41:31,489 --> 00:41:33,059
Perhaps.

758
00:41:33,123 --> 00:41:36,764
So I got a very great idea.

759
00:41:36,794 --> 00:41:39,172
Let's get together
all the sleeping money.

760
00:41:39,196 --> 00:41:44,236
I think if we get it back to the society
it'll be very helpful for Japan.

761
00:41:44,301 --> 00:41:46,247
Maybe!

762
00:41:47,538 --> 00:41:49,279
So, Doraemon...

763
00:41:49,306 --> 00:41:50,876
I want to do something for Japan.

764
00:41:50,941 --> 00:41:52,249
Just bring out this kind of tools.

765
00:41:52,276 --> 00:41:54,779
You did know how to talk!

766
00:41:54,845 --> 00:41:57,689
As what you said,
I can't refuse you at all.

767
00:42:00,518 --> 00:42:02,520
What's that?

768
00:42:06,090 --> 00:42:07,433
Bees...

769
00:42:07,458 --> 00:42:09,870
Doraemon, I'll be bitten.
The bees...

770
00:42:09,894 --> 00:42:11,464
It doesn't matter.

771
00:42:11,529 --> 00:42:14,772
They are the Money Bees.
They won't bite you.

772
00:42:15,766 --> 00:42:17,507
Money Bees.

773
00:42:17,535 --> 00:42:19,412
Money...

774
00:42:19,436 --> 00:42:22,883
It found...

775
00:42:22,907 --> 00:42:25,114
The money...

776
00:42:25,142 --> 00:42:27,349
They'll find the money
on the ground and take it back.

777
00:42:27,378 --> 00:42:30,188
They're the bees which will take money
back to home and store it up.

778
00:42:30,214 --> 00:42:32,057
These guys are really awesome.

779
00:42:32,082 --> 00:42:34,528
So let them start to work now!

780
00:42:36,487 --> 00:42:40,060
You bees,
there's no any money in this house,

781
00:42:40,124 --> 00:42:44,971
just go outside to find money
and take back to this box.

782
00:42:46,864 --> 00:42:49,936
These bees will work very hard.

783
00:42:50,701 --> 00:42:53,807
Let me go outside and watch
how they'll work hard.

784
00:43:03,080 --> 00:43:04,821
Money...

785
00:43:04,848 --> 00:43:07,590
Very good...just like this...

786
00:43:09,587 --> 00:43:11,658
It found...1000 yen...

787
00:43:11,722 --> 00:43:15,033
Bees, you're really very outstanding!

788
00:43:15,526 --> 00:43:20,737
It found it...money...

789
00:43:20,764 --> 00:43:22,971
Go to it...

790
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:27,210
It found it...

791
00:43:27,237 --> 00:43:28,614
Money...

792
00:43:28,639 --> 00:43:29,709
Found it.

793
00:43:29,773 --> 00:43:30,808
Found it...

794
00:43:30,874 --> 00:43:32,410
Money...

795
00:43:32,476 --> 00:43:33,784
Take it back...

796
00:43:33,811 --> 00:43:37,315
So awesome!
They could find money in such a place.

797
00:43:37,381 --> 00:43:39,418
It sure is the Money Bees.

798
00:43:43,020 --> 00:43:45,296
They've gathered so much money.

799
00:43:45,322 --> 00:43:48,769
It only took 30 minutes.

800
00:43:48,826 --> 00:43:52,603
In this case maybe we'll gather dozens
of thousand, no, hundreds of thousand

801
00:43:52,630 --> 00:43:55,509
no, perhaps after a while
we'll gather dozens of million!

802
00:43:55,532 --> 00:43:58,706
Our house need to be rebuilt.
And I want to go abroad for travel.

803
00:43:58,736 --> 00:44:00,215
You can't!

804
00:44:00,270 --> 00:44:03,513
But Mom, this is the money
being lost on the ground.

805
00:44:03,540 --> 00:44:05,713
What's wrong with that? Right, Mom?

806
00:44:05,743 --> 00:44:07,586
Even it's so, but you can't either.

807
00:44:07,611 --> 00:44:09,591
If you don't hand the money which
you picked up to the police station,

808
00:44:09,647 --> 00:44:12,992
that's just committing a crime of
usurping on the fairy money.

809
00:44:13,017 --> 00:44:14,997
What?

810
00:44:15,052 --> 00:44:17,464
It can't be...

811
00:44:20,190 --> 00:44:23,228
I came to hand the money
I picked up everywhere.

812
00:44:23,293 --> 00:44:26,934
Such an announce the finding of
lost property will bother us very much.

813
00:44:26,964 --> 00:44:28,602
Why?

814
00:44:28,666 --> 00:44:30,839
I came to hand the money
I picked up so sincerely.

815
00:44:30,868 --> 00:44:32,870
Why will it bother you so much?

816
00:44:32,936 --> 00:44:38,682
Since the finding of lost property
must confirm the place and amount.

817
00:44:38,709 --> 00:44:41,815
Then you can come to make an
announce the finding of lost property.

818
00:44:41,879 --> 00:44:45,326
As what you said,
there's no any method, eh?

819
00:44:45,382 --> 00:44:47,521
Very sorry, because it's a rule.

820
00:44:47,584 --> 00:44:50,360
Please recall again. Then hand it here.

821
00:44:51,922 --> 00:44:53,799
I took the money to make an announce
the finding of lost property.

822
00:44:53,824 --> 00:44:55,599
Really...

823
00:45:01,031 --> 00:45:04,103
Doraemon,
what will we do with the money?

824
00:45:04,168 --> 00:45:07,047
What 'what'? How to do?

825
00:45:07,071 --> 00:45:10,109
Never thought it would become like this.

826
00:45:10,174 --> 00:45:14,020
Where did we pick up the money?
We'd tell the certain place and amount.

827
00:45:14,044 --> 00:45:16,650
How could we know?

828
00:45:16,914 --> 00:45:21,385
Right, in this case, just ask the bees
to return the money.

829
00:45:21,452 --> 00:45:25,195
But don't you think it's regrettable
for the money picked up hardy.

830
00:45:25,222 --> 00:45:29,102
That's better than committing a crime of
usurping on the fairy money.

831
00:45:29,126 --> 00:45:31,436
It's true.

832
00:45:31,462 --> 00:45:33,999
No way, so we can only give up.

833
00:45:37,901 --> 00:45:39,812
I really feel very sorry for you.

834
00:45:39,837 --> 00:45:42,681
Please return the money to
where you found it.

835
00:45:47,177 --> 00:45:48,952
What?

836
00:45:52,149 --> 00:45:54,789
The bees seem to be very puzzled.

837
00:46:07,030 --> 00:46:08,373
That's bad.

838
00:46:08,398 --> 00:46:12,574
The bees become very angry
since we got them puzzled.

839
00:46:17,174 --> 00:46:18,653
Help!

840
00:46:18,675 --> 00:46:20,916
I'm sorry...

841
00:46:26,717 --> 00:46:30,563
Delivery Bag

842
00:46:40,297 --> 00:46:43,107
Hey, don't get so upset!

843
00:46:43,133 --> 00:46:44,874
It's all in a day's work.

844
00:46:44,902 --> 00:46:46,677
Let's go...

845
00:46:53,243 --> 00:46:56,315
Nobita, you're blamed by your
teacher in the school, right?

846
00:46:56,380 --> 00:47:00,351
Yes, I was blamed by my teacher.
Mom, how could you know?

847
00:47:00,417 --> 00:47:02,226
It stands to reason.

848
00:47:02,252 --> 00:47:04,528
You've forgotten your books
and notebooks at home.

849
00:47:04,555 --> 00:47:07,331
You'd prepare the books and notebooks
for the next day once you get home.

850
00:47:07,357 --> 00:47:09,803
So you do it before me today.

851
00:47:09,827 --> 00:47:11,306
Okay.

852
00:47:12,029 --> 00:47:14,339
I forgot my bag at the school.

853
00:47:14,364 --> 00:47:15,900
Nobita

854
00:47:15,966 --> 00:47:18,446
Why can you be like this?!

855
00:47:19,803 --> 00:47:22,579
I have to do something.

856
00:47:22,606 --> 00:47:25,416
What, forgot again?

857
00:47:25,709 --> 00:47:30,021
Please...give me some medicine
which can make me not forget anything.

858
00:47:30,047 --> 00:47:32,391
You should try your best to
do that occasionally.

859
00:47:32,416 --> 00:47:35,158
Just because I can't,
so I came to ask you.

860
00:47:35,185 --> 00:47:37,995
Forget it, I won't ask you.

861
00:47:38,021 --> 00:47:41,468
Right, I got a good idea to
deal with the amnesia.

862
00:47:41,491 --> 00:47:42,526
Really?

863
00:47:42,593 --> 00:47:44,573
What's that?

864
00:47:44,628 --> 00:47:46,699
Very simple.

865
00:47:47,397 --> 00:47:49,399
That's okay!

866
00:47:49,466 --> 00:47:51,844
Keeping this,
you won't forget to take anything.

867
00:47:51,869 --> 00:47:52,847
Yes!

868
00:47:52,903 --> 00:47:56,646
If you forget to take something,
you'll remember it when you see it.

869
00:47:56,673 --> 00:47:59,449
So it is! I'll remember it when I see it

870
00:47:59,476 --> 00:48:00,853
Someone ask me to do something.

871
00:48:00,878 --> 00:48:02,323
Thank you, Doraemon.

872
00:48:02,346 --> 00:48:04,383
I'll buy the Rice Cracker for you
when I return.

873
00:48:04,448 --> 00:48:07,088
Thank you very much!

874
00:48:07,150 --> 00:48:08,652
So I'm going to play!

875
00:48:08,719 --> 00:48:11,325
Nobita is really a good kid.

876
00:48:12,522 --> 00:48:14,331
What a good time!

877
00:48:14,358 --> 00:48:17,271
I was in Shizuka's home and
asked her to treat me.

878
00:48:17,294 --> 00:48:19,968
That cake really tasted good.

879
00:48:19,997 --> 00:48:23,103
That...gift for me is where?

880
00:48:23,166 --> 00:48:25,146
Gift'?

881
00:48:25,168 --> 00:48:28,706
You tied a rope on your little
finger before you left.

882
00:48:28,772 --> 00:48:31,412
And promised me to buy the
Rice Cracker for me, didn't you?

883
00:48:31,475 --> 00:48:32,749
Right!

884
00:48:32,776 --> 00:48:35,723
It disappeared, where did it fall?

885
00:48:35,746 --> 00:48:39,592
You're really a talent of forgetting.

886
00:48:39,616 --> 00:48:42,062
So that bothered everyone.

887
00:48:42,085 --> 00:48:44,691
Such a person like you need use...

888
00:48:44,755 --> 00:48:46,860
the Delivery Bag.

889
00:48:46,924 --> 00:48:49,336
So you walk with this bag.

890
00:48:49,359 --> 00:48:50,667
What's it?

891
00:48:50,694 --> 00:48:52,833
I just forgot things occasionally,
then you put it over on me!

892
00:48:52,896 --> 00:48:54,807
Don't look down on me!
I'm a boy all to nothing!

893
00:48:54,831 --> 00:48:56,401
How can I take this with me?!

894
00:48:56,466 --> 00:48:58,275
Listen to me!

895
00:48:58,302 --> 00:49:01,408
For an example, if you forget to
take your notebooks home,

896
00:49:01,471 --> 00:49:07,114
then you'll put your hand in the bag as
you're speaking 'my notebooks'.

897
00:49:09,680 --> 00:49:13,184
What's the result? You'll bring out
your notebooks from the bag.

898
00:49:13,250 --> 00:49:15,594
Very good, it's very good.

899
00:49:15,619 --> 00:49:17,963
In this case, no matter how far
I leave my things,

900
00:49:17,988 --> 00:49:20,525
I'll bring them out from this bag.

901
00:49:20,590 --> 00:49:24,504
Anyway bring out your schoolbag left
at the school!

902
00:49:24,528 --> 00:49:26,508
My schoolbag!

903
00:49:26,563 --> 00:49:28,270
It appears!

904
00:49:28,298 --> 00:49:31,177
So even if you forget something,
it'll be nothing serious.

905
00:49:32,002 --> 00:49:33,504
Awesome!

906
00:49:33,570 --> 00:49:36,244
Okay! I'll show it to everyone!

907
00:49:36,273 --> 00:49:38,446
He goes beyond himself at once!

908
00:49:42,846 --> 00:49:46,453
Miss Nobita,
you look very cute with the bag!

909
00:49:46,516 --> 00:49:48,359
Are you going to play?

910
00:49:48,385 --> 00:49:49,864
So cute!

911
00:49:49,886 --> 00:49:53,561
Did you put a doll in it?

912
00:49:53,590 --> 00:49:55,501
But it's not like what you thought.

913
00:49:55,525 --> 00:49:58,005
I'll show you the very wonderful magic.

914
00:49:58,028 --> 00:49:59,268
What?

915
00:49:59,296 --> 00:50:01,276
He said he would perform the magic.
ls that for sure?

916
00:50:01,298 --> 00:50:02,402
Yes.

917
00:50:02,466 --> 00:50:05,072
I can bring out anything
from this bag for you.

918
00:50:05,135 --> 00:50:08,548
He said he would perform the magic!
Also for me!

919
00:50:08,572 --> 00:50:11,052
Then just be quickly!

920
00:50:11,074 --> 00:50:13,145
So let me bring out some snacks first!

921
00:50:13,210 --> 00:50:15,816
My snacks!

922
00:50:17,014 --> 00:50:17,924
A thief!

923
00:50:17,948 --> 00:50:20,053
It hurts...l got hit.

924
00:50:20,117 --> 00:50:21,562
It hurts! Geez!

925
00:50:21,585 --> 00:50:23,394
What?! I failed in the end!

926
00:50:23,420 --> 00:50:27,527
Okay, the next is mom's glasses.
Mom's glasses.

927
00:50:29,526 --> 00:50:30,869
What do you want to do?

928
00:50:30,894 --> 00:50:32,874
Look, this is mom's glasses.

929
00:50:32,896 --> 00:50:34,773
Great...

930
00:50:34,798 --> 00:50:36,106
What?! I failed in the end!

931
00:50:36,133 --> 00:50:38,272
It stands to reason that you bring
out something from the bag.

932
00:50:38,335 --> 00:50:41,339
If you're performing the magic,
just bring out something rare.

933
00:50:41,405 --> 00:50:43,851
All right, now that you said this,

934
00:50:43,874 --> 00:50:46,081
I'll bring out that.

935
00:50:46,109 --> 00:50:48,555
Do you know what this is?

936
00:50:48,578 --> 00:50:50,649
Only a book!

937
00:50:50,714 --> 00:50:53,923
Seems that I've seen it somewhere.

938
00:50:53,950 --> 00:50:55,395
Then I'm reading!

939
00:50:55,419 --> 00:50:56,864
3rd Mar. Sunny

940
00:50:56,887 --> 00:51:01,336
I was looking at myself in the mirror.
How could my face be so pretty?

941
00:51:01,391 --> 00:51:03,928
Stop reading! Isn't that my diary?

942
00:51:07,364 --> 00:51:09,173
You're really a bad kid!

943
00:51:09,199 --> 00:51:11,611
When did you steal this book
from his home?

944
00:51:11,635 --> 00:51:15,105
I didn't steal! I said it to you,
it's the magic.

945
00:51:15,172 --> 00:51:19,416
Really, anyone can perform
this kind of magic, am I right?

946
00:51:19,443 --> 00:51:22,515
Yes! Only if we put things in the bag
in advance.

947
00:51:22,579 --> 00:51:24,388
That's right!

948
00:51:25,282 --> 00:51:28,752
Nobita...you did do like this, eh?

949
00:51:29,386 --> 00:51:32,458
Okay, I'll bring out something else
to show you.

950
00:51:38,995 --> 00:51:40,838
What, isn't that the mat?

951
00:51:40,864 --> 00:51:42,605
What's wrong with the mat?

952
00:51:42,632 --> 00:51:44,043
It's wetted!

953
00:51:44,067 --> 00:51:47,139
This is the welcome mat of Gian's home.

954
00:51:50,841 --> 00:51:54,948
Nobita, you bastard! Wait, don't run!

955
00:51:57,214 --> 00:52:00,821
Glasses...my glasses.

956
00:52:00,884 --> 00:52:02,227
Where is it?

957
00:52:02,252 --> 00:52:04,425
Did I put it there and forget
to take back?

958
00:52:05,422 --> 00:52:09,598
Nobita, my glasses was gone!
Help me to look for it.

959
00:52:09,626 --> 00:52:12,835
Okay, there'll be no problem
with this bag.

960
00:52:12,863 --> 00:52:17,403
I'll bring out mom's glasses
from the bag to show you.

961
00:52:17,467 --> 00:52:20,107
Mom's glasses, return you.

962
00:52:21,071 --> 00:52:22,709
Thanks.

963
00:52:25,976 --> 00:52:27,978
Nobita, you made a practical joke again.

964
00:52:28,044 --> 00:52:29,022
Sorry.

965
00:52:29,045 --> 00:52:30,524
Don't run!

966
00:52:32,649 --> 00:52:36,529
With this, no matter where you go...

967
00:52:39,756 --> 00:52:42,828
What a convenient bag!
So lend me to use for a while.

968
00:52:42,893 --> 00:52:46,602
After all the bag is more
suitable for mom to use.

